      "name": "Teacher (narrator)",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.9
    },
    "D": {
      "name": "Daniel",
      "voice": "am_michael",
      "speed": 0.93
    },
    "M": {
      "name": "Maya",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "speed": 0.93
    },
    "S": {
      "name": "Sofia",
      "voice": "af_nicole",
      "speed": 1.05
    }
  },
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "story",
      "label": "Past and now"
    },
    {
      "id": "form",
      "label": "Form"
    },
    {
      "id": "negq",
      "label": "No and ?"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp",
      "label": "Experience"
    },
    {
      "id": "result",
      "label": "Result"
    },
    {
      "id": "still",
      "label": "Still true"
    },
    {
      "id": "period",
      "label": "Today"
    },
    {
      "id": "finished",
      "label": "Past time"
    },
    {
      "id": "notes",
      "label": "Notes"
    },
    {
      "id": "review",
      "label": "Review"
    }
  ],
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "title",
      "ch": "story",
      "pre": 0.6,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "t1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Welcome to Fluent English. Today, we're learning the present perfect.",
          "nocap": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "story1",
      "ch": "story",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "s1a",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Daniel is at the office door. He's looking for his keys."
        },
        {
          "id": "s1b",
          "kind": "thought",
          "who": "D",
          "text": "Where are my keys?",
          "hold": 2.4
        },
        {
          "id": "s1c",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "D",
          "text": "Oh no! I've lost my keys!",
          "say": "Oh no! [I've](/ˈaɪv/) lost my keys!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "contrast",
      "ch": "story",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "c2",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "I lost my keys yesterday.",
          "say": "I lost my keys yesterday."
        },
        {
          "id": "c3",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "We name a finished time: yesterday. This is the simple past."
        },
        {
          "id": "c4",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "I've lost my keys.",
          "say": "[I've](/ˈaɪv/) lost my keys."
        },
        {
          "id": "c5",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Now the focus is the present result. Here, the keys are missing now."
        },
        {
          "id": "c6",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "The present perfect connects the past to now."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "form1",
      "ch": "form",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "f1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "The form is: subject, plus have or has, plus the past participle."
        },
        {
          "id": "f2",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "She has finished."
        },
        {
          "id": "f3",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "I, you, we, and they use have. He, she, and it use has."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "form2",
      "ch": "form",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "f4",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "The past participle is the third verb form. It is not always the simple past."
        },
        {
          "id": "f5",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Work, worked, worked. See, saw, seen. Go, went, gone. Be, was, been. Eat, ate, eaten.",
          "speed": 0.85
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "form3",
      "ch": "form",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "f7",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "I've finished. She's finished.",
          "say": "[I've](/ˈaɪv/) finished. She's finished."
        },
        {
          "id": "f8",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Here, apostrophe s means has. It can also mean is, so check the next word."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "chk1",
      "ch": "form",
      "check": 1,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "k1q",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Quick check one. She, blank, finished the report. Have, has, or does?",
          "nocap": true
        },
        {
          "id": "k1h",
          "kind": "hold",
          "hold": 6.0
        },
        {
          "id": "k1a",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Has. She is third person singular: she has finished.",
          "nocap": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "neg",
      "ch": "negq",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "n1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "For negatives, put not after have or has. Haven't. Hasn't."
        },
        {
          "id": "n2",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "I haven't finished. She hasn't finished."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "quest",
      "ch": "negq",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "q1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "For questions, put have or has before the subject."
        },
        {
          "id": "q2",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Have you finished? Has she finished?"
        },
        {
          "id": "q3",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "We do not use do or does to make these questions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "short",
      "ch": "negq",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "a1",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "M",
          "text": "Have you eaten lunch?"
        },
        {
          "id": "a2",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "D",
          "text": "Yes, I have."
        },
        {
          "id": "a3",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "M",
          "text": "Has Sofia called?"
        },
        {
          "id": "a4",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "D",
          "text": "No, she hasn't."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "wh",
      "ch": "negq",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "w1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "With question words, put have or has next, before the subject."
        },
        {
          "id": "w2",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "What have you done? How long have you lived here?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "chk2",
      "ch": "negq",
      "check": 2,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "k2q",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Quick check two. Maya has already, blank, lunch. Ate, eaten, or eat?",
          "nocap": true
        },
        {
          "id": "k2h",
          "kind": "hold",
          "hold": 6.0
        },
        {
          "id": "k2a",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Eaten. After has, we need the past participle: has eaten.",
          "nocap": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "exp1",
      "ch": "exp",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "e1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Use one: experience up to now. We don't say when."
        },
        {
          "id": "e2",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "S",
          "text": "Have you ever visited Canada?"
        },
        {
          "id": "e3",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "D",
          "text": "Yes, I have. I visited Canada in 2022.",
          "say": "Yes, I have. I visited Canada in twenty twenty-two."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "exp2",
      "ch": "exp",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "e4",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "First, the experience: present perfect. Then a finished time: simple past."
        },
        {
          "id": "e5",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Never means: not at any time, up to now."
        },
        {
          "id": "e6",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "I've never visited Canada.",
          "say": "[I've](/ˈaɪv/) never visited Canada."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "res1",
      "ch": "result",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "r1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Use two: a recent action with a result now."
        },
        {
          "id": "r2",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "D",
          "text": "Have you finished yet?"
        },
        {
          "id": "r3",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "M",
          "text": "Yes! I've already finished the report.",
          "say": "Yes! [I've](/ˈaɪv/) already finished the report."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "res2",
      "ch": "result",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "r4",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "The report is finished, and it is ready now."
        },
        {
          "id": "r5",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Already goes before the participle. Yet goes at the end."
        },
        {
          "id": "r6",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "I haven't finished yet."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "still1",
      "ch": "still",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "u1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Use three: a situation that began in the past and continues now."
        },
        {
          "id": "u2",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "D",
          "text": "I've known her for five years.",
          "say": "[I've](/ˈaɪv/) known her for five years."
        },
        {
          "id": "u3",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "S",
          "text": "And she's lived here since 2021.",
          "say": "And she's lived here since twenty twenty-one."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "still2",
      "ch": "still",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "u4",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "For introduces a length of time. Since introduces the starting point."
        },
        {
          "id": "u5",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Careful: for and since do not always mean present perfect. A finished situation uses the simple past."
        },
        {
          "id": "u6",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "She lived in Paris for two years."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "chk3",
      "ch": "still",
      "check": 3,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "k3q",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Quick check three. Daniel has worked here, blank, 2019. For, or since?",
          "say": "Quick check three. Daniel has worked here, blank, twenty nineteen. For, or since?",
          "nocap": true
        },
        {
          "id": "k3h",
          "kind": "hold",
          "hold": 6.0
        },
        {
          "id": "k3a",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Since. 2019 is the starting point, not a length of time.",
          "say": "Since. Twenty nineteen is the starting point, not a length of time.",
          "nocap": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "per1",
      "ch": "period",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "p1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Use four: a period that is not finished yet, like today, this week, or this year."
        },
        {
          "id": "p2",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "M",
          "text": "I've had two meetings so far today.",
          "say": "[I've](/ˈaɪv/) had two meetings so far today."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "per2",
      "ch": "period",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "p3",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Today is not over, so we use the present perfect. Yesterday is finished, so we use the simple past."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "I had two meetings yesterday."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Advanced note: the speaker's view matters. If you see today as finished, the simple past is also possible."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fin1",
      "ch": "finished",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "x1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Remember: with a finished time, like yesterday, last week, or in 2022, use the simple past.",
          "say": "Remember: with a finished time, like yesterday, last week, or in twenty twenty-two, use the simple past."
        },
        {
          "id": "x2",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "I saw her yesterday."
        },
        {
          "id": "x3",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Not: I've seen her yesterday.",
          "say": "Not: [I've](/ˈaɪv/) seen her yesterday."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "chk4",
      "ch": "finished",
      "check": 4,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "k4q",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Quick check four. Sofia's trip was last summer. We, blank, Canada last summer. Visited, or have visited?",
          "nocap": true
        },
        {
          "id": "k4h",
          "kind": "hold",
          "hold": 6.0
        },
        {
          "id": "k4a",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Visited. Last summer is a finished time, so we use the simple past.",
          "nocap": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "usn",
      "ch": "notes",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "m1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "American English note: the simple past is also common with just, already, and yet. Both are normal."
        },
        {
          "id": "m2",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "I just ate. I already finished. Did you finish yet?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gone",
      "ch": "notes",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "g1",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "D",
          "text": "Where's Sofia?"
        },
        {
          "id": "g2",
          "kind": "dlg",
          "who": "M",
          "text": "She's gone to London."
        },
        {
          "id": "g3",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Gone: she is away, on her trip."
        },
        {
          "id": "g4",
          "kind": "ex",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "She's been to London."
        },
        {
          "id": "g5",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Been: she visited London at some time. This is an experience."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cont",
      "ch": "notes",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "z1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "One more related form, the present perfect continuous, is a separate form. It is not in this lesson."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sum",
      "ch": "review",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "v1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Let's review. Subject, plus have or has, plus the past participle."
        },
        {
          "id": "v2",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Use it for experience, a recent result, a situation that continues, and an unfinished time."
        },
        {
          "id": "v3",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "For a finished time, use the simple past."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "speak",
      "ch": "review",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "y1",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Now it's your turn! Say three sentences. Something you've done today. A place you've never visited. Someone you've known for years.",
          "say": "Now it's your turn! Say three sentences. Something [you've](/jˈuv/) done today. A place [you've](/jˈuv/) never visited. Someone [you've](/jˈuv/) known for years.",
          "nocap": true
        },
        {
          "id": "y2",
          "kind": "hold",
          "hold": 7.0
        },
        {
          "id": "y3",
          "who": "N",
          "text": "Great work. See you in the next lesson!",
          "nocap": true
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}